---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Island from '../components/Island.astro';
import ProductTour from '../components/ProductTour.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import '../styles/landing.css';
import {product} from '../data/site';

---
<Layout title="Floatlet: Free Dynamic Island for Windows 10 & 11" description="Free, open-source Dynamic Island for Windows 10 and 11. Music controls, file tray, timers and PC search in one native app. No signup or subscription.">
<section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
 <div class="hero-copy">
  <p class="hero-kicker"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> A LITTLE MORE FLOW FOR WINDOWS</p>
  <h1 id="hero-title">Dynamic Island.<br/><span>Made for Windows.</span></h1>
  <p class="hero-lead">Your music. That file. A moment to focus.<br/>Floatlet brings the little things together, in one small space on your desktop.</p>
  <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button primary" href="/download/" data-event="download_click" data-placement="hero"><Icon name="windows" size={18}/> Get Floatlet for Windows <Icon name="download" size={18}/></a><a class="hero-source" href={product.repository} data-event="github_click">Free &amp; open source <Icon size={15}/></a></div>
  <p class="hero-note">Windows 10 &amp; 11 · x64 · No account required</p>
  <div class="hero-bottom-note"><span class="mini-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span><p>Small enough to stay out of the way.<br/><strong>Useful enough to keep around.</strong></p></div>
 </div>
 <div class="hero-product" id="experience">
  <div class="product-caption"><span class="caption-line"></span><span>GO ON, MAKE YOURSELF AT HOME</span><Icon name="sliders" size={15}/></div>
  <Island/>
 </div>
</section>
<div class="proof-strip wrap" aria-label="Floatlet facts"><span><Icon name="check" size={17}/> Free to use</span><span><Icon name="code" size={17}/> Native C++</span><span><Icon name="file" size={17}/> MIT licensed</span><span><Icon name="windows" size={17}/> Windows 10 &amp; 11</span><a href="/docs/capabilities/">Explore what it can do <Icon size={15}/></a></div>
<ProductTour/>
<section class="search-showcase wrap" id="search" aria-labelledby="search-title">
 <div class="search-copy"><p class="eyebrow">A THOUGHT. A SHORTCUT.</p><h2 id="search-title">Find it.<br/><span>Keep moving.</span></h2><p>Your apps, indexed files, open windows and Floatlet commands. One shortcut, chosen by you.</p><button class="button secondary" data-search-open><Icon name="search" size={18}/> Try sample Search <Icon size={18}/></button><a class="underlink" href="/docs/search/">How Floatlet Search works <Icon size={15}/></a></div>
 <div class="search-illustration" aria-label="Illustration of Floatlet Search with sample results"><div class="illustration-top"><span><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> FLOATLET SEARCH</span><span>ESC</span></div><div class="illustration-query"><Icon name="search" size={23}/><span>visual studio code</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i></div><p class="illustration-label">APPLICATIONS</p><div class="illustration-result active"><svg width="32" height="32" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="#3ba5f5" d="m23 2 7 3v22l-7 3-16-13-5 4v-6l5-4 16 13V8L7 21l-5-4v-6l5 4Z"/></svg><div><strong>Visual Studio Code</strong><small>Application</small></div><span>↵</span></div><div class="illustration-result"><Icon name="file" size={28}/><div><strong>Project notes.md</strong><small>Sample file</small></div></div><div class="illustration-footer"><span><kbd>↵</kbd> Open</span><span><kbd>⇧ ↵</kbd> Add to tray</span><span><kbd>⇥</kbd> Actions</span></div><p class="illustration-disclaimer">Sample interface. The website does not search your PC.</p></div>
</section>
<section class="open-section wrap" aria-labelledby="open-title">
 <div class="open-visual" aria-hidden="true"><div class="open-orbit orbit-one"></div><div class="open-orbit orbit-two"></div><div class="native-island"><span class="native-note"><Icon name="music" size={25}/></span><span><strong>A slower morning</strong><small>Floatlet Sessions · sample</small></span><div class="native-wave"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div></div><span class="orbit-label label-one"><Icon name="calendar" size={16}/> Your day</span><span class="orbit-label label-two"><Icon name="tray" size={16}/> Your files</span><span class="orbit-label label-three"><Icon name="clock" size={16}/> Your time</span></div>
 <div><p class="eyebrow">MADE FOR YOUR DESKTOP</p><h2 id="open-title">A small footprint.<br/><span>An open project.</span></h2><p>Native C++ and Windows composition, without a bundled browser. Free to use, MIT licensed, and open for you to explore.</p><div class="native-facts"><span><Icon name="check" size={17}/> No subscription</span><span><Icon name="check" size={17}/> Settings stored locally</span></div><a class="underlink" href="/docs/capabilities/">Features, compatibility and preview limits <Icon size={15}/></a><p class="fine">An unsigned x64 preview. Some controls depend on hardware or open Windows settings.</p></div>
</section>
<section class="home-faq wrap" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">BEFORE YOU MAKE ROOM</p><h2 id="faq-title">Good questions.<br/><span>Clear answers.</span></h2><a class="underlink" href="/dynamic-island-for-windows/">Read the Windows guide <Icon size={15}/></a></div><div class="faq">
 <details><summary>Is Floatlet really free?</summary><p>Yes. Floatlet is free to download and its source is available under the MIT license. The current Windows preview does not require an account or subscription.</p></details>
 <details><summary>Will it work on my PC?</summary><p>The x64 preview supports Windows 10 and 11 on Intel and AMD PCs. Windows 11 ARM PCs can use x64 emulation. A native ARM64 download is not available.</p></details>
 <details><summary>Does it work with my music player?</summary><p>Floatlet uses supported Windows media sessions for artwork and playback. Browser behaviour varies. When artwork is missing, the app can look up a matching cover in Apple's catalogue.</p></details>
 <details><summary>Can I connect my calendar?</summary><p>Add up to eight private Google Calendar iCal subscriptions for a merged, read-only agenda and five-minute reminders. Private links stay encrypted for your Windows user.</p></details>
 <details><summary>Does the website access my PC?</summary><p>No. This playground uses sample music, files, search results and fictional events. It does not access your media sessions, personal files, calendar, or Windows settings.</p></details>
</div></section>
<section class="get-it wrap"><div class="download-banner"><div><p class="eyebrow">A LITTLE SPACE. A BETTER FLOW.</p><h2>Make room<br/>for Floatlet.</h2><p>Your desktop companion for the everyday.</p></div><div><a class="button" href="/download/"><Icon name="windows" size={19}/> Get the Windows preview <Icon name="download" size={19}/></a><p>Free · Open source · Windows 10 &amp; 11</p></div><span class="banner-orbit" aria-hidden="true"></span></div></section>
</Layout>